#
# The jobs run.sh makes of the suites, and how long each takes: run.sh starts
# the longest first.  A suite not listed is one job, started last.
#
#   suite   job ("-" when the suite is one)   seconds   environment
#
# A suite that runs its tests under the planner and under ORCA is one job a
# pass, and diskquota's, pax's and resgroup's a job a group of their tests
# too, resgroup's each on a cgroup parent of its own (resgroup/run.sh), as
# singlenode_resgroup's are, the same tests on one node.
# ALONE=1 jobs run after the rest, side by side with each other alone:
# resgroup's test that measures a group's share of the CPU, each pass on
# half the cores (CPUS); and ALONE=2 jobs after those, alone again: the same
# test on one node, on the same cores.  The seconds are a run's, on the
# machine the port is built on (16 cores, 32 threads), with the jobs started
# as the memory let them, ten at once at most; they order the jobs and
# nothing else, and run.sh's summary gives each run's own.
#
# MEM= is the most memory the job holds, in megabytes -- its servers' data,
# WAL and shared memory, /tmp being a tmpfs -- as run.sh's summaries gave
# it, the most of several runs, between which a long job's figure moved 5%
# at most, and some to spare, about 5% and 200 MB: run.sh starts a job only
# while there is that much left for it.  ic_greenplum's and ic_isolation2's
# are from two runs of theirs (CB_IC=all).  The servers keep 64 MB of WAL a
# node, where PostgreSQL keeps up to a gigabyte, but in a group with mirrors
# or a standby (greenplum/run.sh).  More than the summary said for
# resgroup's, whose servers move to cgroup parents outside the job's cgroup,
# where the summary does not see them.
#
# PGPORT= is the first port of a job of the greenplum suite's harness --
# greenplum's, pax_regress's, ic_greenplum's -- whose tcp group's nodes
# listen on 127.0.0.1 (greenplum/run.sh), as the proxies do: two such jobs
# side by side, each taking its ports at random from the same two hundred,
# met on one now and then ("could not bind IPv4 address"), and two of them
# fit in the memory at once.  Sixty apart, each job's nodes' ports its own,
# and above the stand-ins' of pxf_fdw and gpcloud, 7320 to 7719.

resgroup               orca_cpu 103   PASSES=orca RG_GROUPS=cpu ALONE=1 CPUS=16-31 MEM=1500
resgroup               planner_cpu 102 PASSES=planner RG_GROUPS=cpu ALONE=1 CPUS=0-15 MEM=1500
resgroup               orca_cpuset 79 PASSES=orca RG_GROUPS=cpuset MEM=1500
resgroup               planner_cpuset 77 PASSES=planner RG_GROUPS=cpuset MEM=1500
